# .env.example — SAFE TO COMMIT
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and replace placeholders with values
# from your Supabase project settings. NEVER commit the real .env file.
#
# This app is TanStack Start + Vite. A VITE_ prefix means the value MAY be
# exposed in the client bundle (import.meta.env.VITE_*). Only public values
# get that prefix. See docs/env-var-checklist.md and
# docs/sponsor-auth-requirements.md.

# ---- Client-safe (may be used in browser code under RLS) ----
# Public Supabase project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Public anon key (safe in the browser ONLY because RLS policies protect data)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ---- Server-only (MUST NOT be imported into client/browser bundles) ----
# Service role key bypasses RLS. Use only in trusted server code.
# NEVER name this VITE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — Vite would ship it to the browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# Optional: same URL without a VITE_ prefix for server-side reads
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Optional: server-side alias of the anon key (same placeholder as VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY).
# Use in createServerFn / loaders so sponsor listing queries run as the signed-in user.
# This is NOT the service-role key and must never be replaced with it.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ---- Semantic search embeddings (server-only; never VITE_) ----
# Used by src/lib/embeddings/generate.ts. Use `mock` for a labeled 1536-d
# offline vector (not real meaning). Real keys stay in local env only.
EMBEDDING_API_KEY=your-embedding-api-key-here
# Optional. Default is text-embedding-3-small (1536 dimensions).
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# Optional OpenAI-compatible embeddings URL.
# EMBEDDING_API_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/embeddings
